cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the relevant methodological references listed in the documentation."
type: software
title: "blrfit: broad AGN emission lines against the narrow-line systemic velocity"
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ektrnddn/blrfit"
authors:
  - family-names: Dadiani
    given-names: Ekaterine
    affiliation: "Carnegie Mellon University"
    email: edadiani@andrew.cmu.edu
keywords:
  - active galactic nuclei
  - broad emission lines
  - spectroscopy
  - supermassive black hole binaries
  - DESI
  - SDSS
abstract: >-
  Fits the broad Halpha and Hbeta emission-line profiles of AGN spectra, measures
  their offsets from the narrow lines of the same fit, and reports profile classes,
  quality flags and optional Monte Carlo errors. Reads DESI coadds, SDSS spectra
  and spectra in tables or FITS images, and downloads public DESI and SDSS spectra
  by TARGETID or sky position; measures the velocity change of a broad line between
  the dated spectra of one object by a template cross-correlation and sorts objects
  into candidate tiers. Mg II is experimental.
